{"path":"/documentation/schema/request","section":"documentation","title":"request","description":"Documentation for the nnsight Python library","toc":[{"id":"nnsight.schema.request","label":"request","depth":2},{"id":"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel","label":"RequestModel","depth":3}],"segments":[{"type":"html","html":"<h2 id=\"nnsight.schema.request\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-module\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-module-name\">request</span>\n\n\n</h2>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-class\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-class-name\">RequestModel</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p class=\"doc-class-bases\">\n              Bases: <code><span title=\"pydantic.BaseModel\">BaseModel</span></code></p>\n\n\n\n        <p>The JSON routing envelope for a remote request.</p>\n<p>The execution payload (the interventions plus how to invoke the model) is\nnot stored here; <a title=\"            serialize\n\n\n  \n      classmethod\n  \" href=\"#nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.serialize\"><code>serialize</code></a> builds it from a tracer on demand. The\nmodel itself is never carried — it's identified by <code>model_key</code>.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.model_key\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">model_key</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"model_key: str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.session_id\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">session_id</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-class-attribute\"><code>class-attribute</code></small>\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"session_id: str = ''"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.compress\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">compress</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-class-attribute\"><code>class-attribute</code></small>\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"compress: bool = False"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.env\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">env</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-class-attribute\"><code>class-attribute</code></small>\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-instance-attribute\"><code>instance-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"env: dict[str, Any] = {}"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.metadata\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">metadata</span>\n\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"metadata() -> str"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.serialize\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">serialize</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-classmethod\"><code>classmethod</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"serialize(tracer: Any, compress: bool = False) -> bytes"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Turn a tracer into the binary execution payload.</p>\n<p>Reduces the traced block with <a title=\"            reduce_block\" href=\"/documentation/intervention/serialization#nnsight.intervention.serialization.reduce_block\"><code>reduce_block</code></a>\n— its source (unparsed from the tracer's AST) plus only the globals/locals\nit references — so it ships as text rather than version-fragile bytecode,\nand hands that tuple, with the tracer (which carries the model\ninvocation), to the serialization module.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h4 id=\"nnsight.schema.request.RequestModel.deserialize\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-method\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">deserialize</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-staticmethod\"><code>staticmethod</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h4>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"deserialize(blob: bytes, persistent_objects: Optional[dict] = None, compress: bool = False, unpickler: type = CustomCloudUnpickler) -> Any"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Inverse of serialize: rebuild the ready-to-run tracer.</p>\n<p>Recompiles the traced block from its source (under the original\nfilename/name so tracebacks point somewhere sensible) and injects it back\nas <code>tracer.info.code</code>, then restores the captured globals/locals onto\nthe tracer's frame — so the server can run <code>tracer.execute(tracer.info.\ncode)</code> against this actor's live model. The source is also registered in\n<code>linecache</code> so a traceback can show the offending line even though the\nuser's file isn't present on the server.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"}]}